Dear Stephen,

In the median absolute deviation calculation, R by default adjusts by constant scale factor of 1.4826 for asymptotically normal consistency (see ?mad for further details). Could you check to see if this explains the discrepancy in your excel result?

If not, perhaps it would be helpful if you could repeat your calculations on a specific dataset that we both have access to and share your results. The KcViabSmall dataset that is distributed with cellHTS2 is one option. In this way it will be easier for others to pinpoint the source of this discrepancy.

Best wishes,
Joseph

