From fcchan at bccrc.ca  Wed Dec 14 17:40:50 2011
From: fcchan at bccrc.ca (Fong Chun Chan)
Date: Wed, 14 Dec 2011 08:40:50 -0800
Subject: [BioC] Combining 2 different Affychips for analysis e.g.
 HGU133A and HGU133plus2
Message-ID: <83F88080-74E3-4F9E-B1A6-0191528E79AD@bccrc.ca>

Depends on how you want to do it:

1) Can you combine all the samples and then do differential expression? I would argue no because even though the U133A probes are a subset of the U133plus2 probes (I recall reading this), the U133plus2 uses additional probes in each probesets to measure gene expression levels.  So you would be getting different gene expression values for each gene depending on the microarray.

2) Can you do differential expression analysis on each microarray platform by itself, analyze it separately and combine the results?  I think you would probably have more luck and less criticism doing this.  Since they are both microarray platforms made by the same company, Affymetrix, you can have more confidence in combining the results.  This is different from saying comparing the results from RNA-Seq to Microarray since you are dealing with two different platforms and protocols.

Hope that helps!

Fong

